    "body": "Feedback from a hand test of the tool library window on `main` `582981bf` (after #3900 and #3903), macOS. The window works well. Three notes for the next U-series PRs:\n\n1. **Label order on the Document tab.** The label \"Tool type\" is shown below its dropdown. The label \"Name filter\" is shown below \"Tool type\", above its text field. The two labels look out of order. Put each label next to its control (or above it), the same as in the other forms.\n   ![Tool library window: the labels \"Tool type\" and \"Name filter\" below the dropdown](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/issue-3893/tool-window-labels.png?raw=true)\n2. **\"New tool…\" opens the form in the Properties panel**, outside the window. Editing an existing tool now happens in the window (Tool and Details tabs). A new tool can use the same view, so that the two tasks look the same.\n   ![New tool form in the Properties panel, beside the tool library window](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/issue-3893/new-tool-in-properties.png?raw=true)\n3. **The Holder column shows \"-\" and Recipes shows 0** for each tool. This is expected until U4-U6. It is listed here only so that the empty columns are not reported as a bug.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
